    "displayName": "POPE",
    "aliases": ["Polling-based Object Probing Evaluation"],
    "description": "Polling-based Object Probing Evaluation for object hallucination in vision-language models. For each image the model answers yes/no questions of the form \"Is there a {object} in the image?\" under random, popular, and adversarial negative sampling. Scored with accuracy (and often F1) against ground-truth presence labels, commonly on COCO.",
    "summary": "Tests whether the model says an object is in an image when the object is not there.",
